              "uco-observable:stringValue": "Query Reports Utilities Help Log Out\n\nCAT B,CLOSED\n\nU.S. District Court\nDistrict of Columbia (Washington, DC)\nCRIMINAL DOCKET FOR CASE #: 1:23-cr-00064-CJN All Defendants\n\nCase title: USA v. REHMAN Date Filed: 03/02/2023\n\nAssigned to: Judge Carl J. Nichols\n\nDefendant (1)\nJASON HANIF REHMAN represented by JASON HANIF REHMAN\n97366-007\nP.O. Box 2000\nJoint Base MDL, NJ 08640\nPRO SE\n\nEugene Jeen-Young Kim Ohm\nFEDERAL PUBLIC DEFENDER FOR THE DISTRICT OF COLUMBIA\n625 Indiana Avenue, NW\nSuite 550\nWashington, DC 20004\n(202) 208-7500\nFax: (202) 208-7515\nEmail: eugene_ohm@fd.org\nLEAD ATTORNEY\nATTORNEY TO BE NOTICED\nDesignation: Public Defender or Community Defender Appointment\n\nPending Counts Disposition\n18:2422(b); COERCION OR ENTICEMENT OF FEMALE; Coercion and Enticement of a\nDefendant sentenced to One Hundred Sixty-eight (168) months of Incarceration, followed by Ten\nMinor\n(10) years of Supervised Release (with conditions). $100 Special Assessment.\n(1)\n\nHighest Offense Level (Opening)\nFelony\n\nTerminated Counts Disposition\n18:2423(b); COERCION OR ENTICEMENT OF MINOR FEMALE; Travel with Intent to\nEngage in Illicit Sexual Conduct DISMISSED ON GOVERNMENT'S MOTION\n(2)\n18:2251(a) and (e); SEXUAL EXPLOITATION OF CHILDREN; Sexual Exploitation of a Child\nand Attempted Sexual Exploitation of a Child DISMISSED ON GOVERNMENT'S MOTION\n(3)\n18:2252(a)(2) and (b)(1); ACTIVITIES RE MATERIAL CONSTITUTING/CONTAINING\nCHILD PORNO; Attempted Receipt of Child Pornography DISMISSED ON GOVERNMENT'S MOTION\n(4)\n\nHighest Offense Level (Terminated)\nFelony\n\nComplaints Disposition\nNone\n\nPlaintiff\nUSA represented by Angelica Carrasco-Riley\nChild Exploitation and Obscenity Section\n1301 New York Avenue, N.W.\nSuite 11\nWashington D.C., DC 20530\n202-305-4238\nEmail: angelica.carrasco@usdoj.gov\nLEAD ATTORNEY\nATTORNEY TO BE NOTICED\nDesignation: Assistant U.S. Attorney\n\nCaroline Burrell\nU.S. ATTORNEY'S OFFICE\n601 D Street NW\nWashington, DC 20530\n202-815-8613\nEmail: caroline.burrell@usdoj.gov\nLEAD ATTORNEY\nATTORNEY TO BE NOTICED\nDesignation: Assistant U.S. Attorney\n\nShehzad Akhtar\nDOJ-USAO\nDistrict of Columbia (DC)\n555 Fourth Street\nWashington, DC 20001\n(202) 252-7498\nEmail: shehzad.akhtar@usdoj.gov\nLEAD ATTORNEY\nATTORNEY TO BE NOTICED\nDesignation: Assistant U.S. Attorney\n\nRick E. Blaylock , Jr.\nU.S. DEPARTMENT OF JUSTICE\nUnited States Attorney's Office for the District of Col\n601 D Street, NW\nWashington, DC 20004\n202-252-6765\nEmail: rick.blaylock.jr@usdoj.gov\nATTORNEY TO BE NOTICED\n\nDate Filed # Docket Text\n03/02/2023 1 SEALED INDICTMENT as to JASON HANIF REHMAN (1) count(s) 1, 2, 3, 4. (FORFEITURE NOTICE) (zstd) (Entered: 03/03/2023)\n03/02/2023 3 MOTION to Seal Case by USA as to JASON HANIF REHMAN. (Attachments: # 1 Text of Proposed Order)(zstd) (Entered: 03/03/2023)\n03/02/2023 4 ORDER granting 3 Motion to Seal Case as to JASON HANIF REHMAN (1). Signed by Magistrate Judge G. Michael Harvey on 3/2/2023. (zstd) (Entered: 03/03/2023)\n03/07/2023 Arrest of JASON HANIF REHMAN (bb) (Entered: 03/10/2023)\n03/07/2023 6 Arrest Warrant, dated 3/2/2023, Returned Executed on 3/7/2023 as to JASON HANIF REHMAN (1). (bb) (Entered: 03/10/2023)\n03/07/2023 ORAL MOTION to Unseal Case by USA as to JASON HANIF REHMAN (1). (bb) (Entered: 03/10/2023)\n03/07/2023 ORAL MOTION to Appoint Counsel by JASON HANIF REHMAN (1). (bb) (Entered: 03/10/2023)\n03/07/2023 ORAL MOTION for Temporary Detention by USA as to JASON HANIF REHMAN (1). (bb) (Entered: 03/10/2023)\n03/07/2023 Minute Entry for proceedings held before Magistrate Judge G. Michael Harvey: In Person Return on Arrest Warrant/ Initial Appearance/ Arraignment as to JASON HANIF REHMAN (1) Counts 1-4 held on 3/7/2023. Plea\nof Not Guilty entered by JASON HANIF REHMAN (1) as to all counts. Defendant was present in the courtroom. Oral Motion by the Government to Unseal Case as to JASON HANIF REHMAN (1); Heard and Granted.\nCase ordered UNSEALED. Oral Motion to Appoint Counsel by JASON HANIF REHMAN (1); Heard and Granted. FPD, Eugene Ohm was appointed for JASON HANIF REHMAN (1). The Court advised the\nGovernment of its due process obligations under Rule 5(f). Oral Motion by the Government for Temporary Detention (3-day hold) as to JASON HANIF REHMAN (1); Heard and Granted. Detention Hearing set for\n3/13/2023 at 1:00 PM in Courtroom 4- In Person before Magistrate Judge Zia M. Faruqui. Bond Status of Defendant: Committed/Commitment Issued; Court Reporter: FTR Gold; FTR Time Frame: CTRM 6 [2:51:27-\n3:03:09]; Defense Attorney: Eugene Ohm; U.S. Attorney: Caroline Burrell; Pretrial Officer: Britney Dahlkoetter. (bb) (Entered: 03/10/2023)\n03/07/2023 MINUTE ORDER as to JASON HANIF REHMAN (1): As required by Rule 5(f), the United States is ordered to produce all exculpatory evidence to the defendant pursuant to Brady v. Maryland and its progeny. Not doing\nso in a timely manner may result in sanctions, including exclusion of evidence, adverse jury instructions, dismissal of charges and contempt proceedings. Signed by Magistrate Judge G. Michael Harvey on 3/7/2023. (bb)\n(Entered: 03/10/2023)\n03/07/2023 Case unsealed as to JASON HANIF REHMAN. (zcll) (Entered: 03/13/2023)\n03/10/2023 7 NOTICE OF ATTORNEY APPEARANCE Angelica Carrasco-Riley appearing for USA. (zstd) (Entered: 03/10/2023)\n03/13/2023 ORAL MOTION to Commit Defendant to Custody of Attorney General by USA as to JASON HANIF REHMAN. (znjb) (Entered: 03/14/2023)\n03/13/2023 ORAL MOTION for Release from Custody by JASON HANIF REHMAN. (znjb) (Entered: 03/14/2023)\n03/13/2023 Minute Entry for proceedings held before Magistrate Judge Zia M. Faruqui: Detention Hearing as to JASON HANIF REHMAN held on 3/13/2023. Defendant present in the courtroom. Continued Detention Hearing set for\n3/15/2023 at 12:00 PM in Courtroom 4- In Person before Magistrate Judge Zia M. Faruqui. Status Hearing set for 3/16/2023 at 3:15 PM in Courtroom 19- In Person before Judge Carl J. Nichols. Bond Status of Defendant:\nDefendant Held Without Bond; Court Reporter: FTR- GOLD; FTR Time Frame: CRTM 4: [1:37:25-2:35:06]; Defense Attorney: Eugene Ohm; US Attorney: Angelica Carrasco-Riley and Caroline Burrell; Pretrial Officer:\nJohn Copes. Witnesses: Rick Shahini- Uncle (znjb) Modified on 3/14/2023 (znjb). (Entered: 03/14/2023)\n03/15/2023 ORAL MOTION for Speedy Trial by USA as to JASON HANIF REHMAN. (znjb) (Entered: 03/15/2023)\n03/15/2023 Minute Entry for proceedings held before Magistrate Judge Zia M. Faruqui: Continued Detention Hearing as to JASON HANIF REHMAN held on 3/15/2023. Defendant present in the courtroom. Oral Motion by the\nGovernment to Commit Defendant to Custody of Attorney General as to JASON HANIF REHMAN; heard and denied. Oral Motion for Release from Custody as to JASON HANIF REHMAN; heard and granted.\nDefendant released to Home Incarceration/3rd Party Custodian. Defendant to be released on 3/16/2023 from the District Court cell block. Oral Motion by the Government for Speedy Trial as to JASON HANIF REHMAN;\nheard and granted. Speedy Trial Excluded between 3/15/2023 to 3/16/2023 in the Interest of Justice (XT). Bond Status of Defendant: Defendant Release/3rd Party Custodian; Court Reporter: FTR- GOLD; FTR Time\nFrame: CRTM 4: [12:20:19-1:25:22]; Defense Attorney: Eugene Ohm; US Attorney: Angelica Carrasco-Riley and Caroline Burrell; Pretrial Officer: Andre Sidbury; 3rd Party Custodians: Laurie Shaw- Sister and Erin\nRehamn- Sister in Law. (znjb) (Entered: 03/15/2023)\n03/15/2023 9 ORDER Setting Conditions for High Intensity Supervision Program as to JASON HANIF REHMAN (1) HISP. Signed by Magistrate Judge Zia M. Faruqui on 3/15/2023. (Attachments: # 1 Appearance Bond) (zcll)\n(Entered: 03/16/2023)\n03/16/2023 8 Unopposed MOTION for Protective Order re Discovery by USA as to JASON HANIF REHMAN. (Burrell, Caroline) (Entered: 03/16/2023)\n03/16/2023 MINUTE ORDER as to JASON HANIF REHMAN: As discussed at the Detention Hearing on March 15, 2023, the Court directed defense counsel to have Mr. Shahani call chambers to be sworn in as an additional third-\nparty custodian. On March 16, 2023, the Court received a call from Mr. Shahani. The Court swore Mr. Shahani in as a third-party custodian after reviewing the conditions of release with him. Signed by Magistrate Judge\nZia M. Faruqui on 3/16/2023. (ztl) (Entered: 03/16/2023)\n03/16/2023 10 Unopposed MOTION for Order re Discovery by USA as to JASON HANIF REHMAN. (Burrell, Caroline) Modified event type on 3/16/2023 (zstd). (Entered: 03/16/2023)\n03/16/2023 Minute Entry for proceedings held Via Video before Judge Carl J. Nichols:Status Conference as to JASON HANIF REHMAN held on 3/16/2023. Defendant Consents To This Hearing Being Held Via Video (ZOOM).\nParties Request Forty-Five (45) Day Continuance. Status Conference set for 5/3/2023 at 2:00 PM in Telephonic/VTC before Judge Carl J. Nichols. With The Consent Of The Parties, Speedy Trial Time Is Excluded 3/16/23\n- 5/3/23 In The Interest Of Justice (XT). If The Status Conference Is Converted To A Change Of Plea Hearing, The Change Of Plea Hearing Will Be In-Person And Submit Plea Documents To The Court By No Later Than\nApril 28, 2023. Bond Status of Defendant: APPEARED REMOTELY - VIA VIDEO- ZOOM; REMAINS IN HIGH INTENSITY SUPERVISION PROGRAM; Court Reporter: LISA EDWARDS; Defense Attorney:\nEUGENE OHM; US Attorney: CAROLINE BURRELL; (mac) (Entered: 03/16/2023)\n03/27/2023 11 Protective Order as to JASON HANIF REHMAN. Signed by Judge Carl J. Nichols on March 27, 2023. (lccjn2) Modified on 4/17/2023 to add defendant's name (zcdw). (Entered: 03/27/2023)\n03/27/2023 MINUTE ORDER as to JASON HANIF REHMAN. Upon review of the Government's 10 Unopposed Motion to Disclose Items Protected by Federal Rule of Criminal Procedure 6(e), it is ORDERED that the Motion is\nGRANTED. The Government may provide in discovery materials protected by Federal Rule of Criminal Procedure 6(e). It is further ORDERED that the Government may provide in discovery sealed materials pursuant to\nthe protective order governing discovery. Signed by Judge Carl J. Nichols on March 27, 2023. (lccjn2) (Entered: 03/27/2023)\n04/13/2023 12 NOTICE re Discovery Filing by USA as to JASON HANIF REHMAN (Burrell, Caroline) (Entered: 04/13/2023)\n05/01/2023 13 Joint MOTION to Continue Status Hearing, Joint MOTION to Exclude Time by USA as to JASON HANIF REHMAN. (Burrell, Caroline) (Entered: 05/01/2023)\n05/01/2023 MINUTE ORDER as to JASON HANIF REHMAN. Upon review of the 13 Joint Motion to Continue and Exclude Time, it is ORDERED that the Motion is GRANTED. The status conference scheduled for May 3, 2023 is\nVACATED and RESCHEDULED for July 11, 2023 at 2:00 PM via video conference. It is further ORDERED that the interests of justice are best served and outweigh the interests of the public and the Defendant in a\nspeedy trial, and the time from May 3, 2023, through July 11, 2023, shall be excluded in computing the time in which trial must commence in this case under the Speedy Trial Act. Signed by Judge Carl J. Nichols on May\n1, 2023. (lccjn2) (Entered: 05/01/2023)\n05/24/2023 14 Unopposed MOTION to Modify Conditions of Release by JASON HANIF REHMAN. (Attachments: # 1 Text of Proposed Order)(Ohm, Eugene) (Entered: 05/24/2023)\n05/31/2023 MINUTE ORDER as to JASON HANIF REHMAN. Upon review of the Defendant's 14 Unopposed Motion to Modify Conditions of Release, it is ORDERED that the Motion is GRANTED. It is further ORDERED that\nthe Defendant's conditions of release are MODIFIED to authorize him to perform duties outside of his house, specifically to include taking out trash and recycling and lawn maintenance, provided that he is under the visual\nmonitoring of a third-party custodian and he remains on the property. Signed by Judge Carl J. Nichols on May 31, 2023. (lccjn2) (Entered: 05/31/2023)\n07/11/2023 Minute Entry for proceedings held Via Video (ZOOM) before Judge Carl J. Nichols:Status Conference as to JASON HANIF REHMAN held Via Video (ZOOM) on 7/11/2023. The Defendant Consents To This Hearing\nBeing Held Via Video. Parties Updated The Court About Plea Offer. Parties Request Ninety (90) Day Continuance. Further Status Conference set for 10/6/2023 at 1:00 PM Via Video (ZOOM) before Judge Carl J. Nichols.\nWith The Consent Of The Parties, Speedy Trial Time Is Excluded 7/11/2023 - 10/06/2023 In The Interest Of Justice (XT). Bond Status of Defendant: APPEARED VIA VIDEO - REMAINS ON PERSONAL\nRECOGNIZANCE; Court Reporter: LORRAINE HERMAN; Defense Attorney: EUGENE OHM; US Attorney: CAROLINE BURRELL/ ANGELICA CARRASCO-RILEY; (mac) (Entered: 07/11/2023)\n10/04/2023 16 Consent MOTION to Continue Status Hearing, Consent MOTION to Exclude Time Under the Speedy Trial Act by JASON HANIF REHMAN. (Attachments: # 1 Text of Proposed Order)(Ohm, Eugene) (Entered:\n10/04/2023)\n10/06/2023 MINUTE ORDER as to JASON REHMAN. Upon review of the 16 Joint Motion to Continue Status Conference and Exclude Time Under the Speedy Trial Act, it is ORDERED that the Motion is GRANTED. It is further\nORDERED that the status conference is continued until December 7, 2023 at 12:30 PM. It is further ORDERED that the period from October 6, 2023 and December 7, 2023 be excluded from computing the time within\nwhich a trial must commence under the Speedy Trial Act because the ends of justice served by such a continuance outweigh the interests of the public and Defendant in a speedy trial. SO ORDERED by Judge Carl J.\nNichols on October 6, 2023. (lccjn2) (Entered: 10/06/2023)\n10/13/2023 18 Unopposed MOTION to Modify Conditions of Release by JASON HANIF REHMAN. (Attachments: # 1 Text of Proposed Order)(Ohm, Eugene) (Entered: 10/13/2023)\n10/17/2023 MINUTE ORDER as to JASON HANIF REHMAN. The Parties are ordered to appear for a hearing on Monday October 23 at 10:00 A.M. to discuss the 18 Unopposed Motion to Modify Conditions of Release. So\nORDERED by Judge Carl J. Nichols on October 17, 2023. (lccjn2) (Entered: 10/17/2023)\n10/18/2023 Set/Reset Hearings as to JASON HANIF REHMAN: Motion Hearing reset for 10/23/2023 at 11:00 AM in Courtroom 17- In Person before Judge Carl J. Nichols. (zcam) (Entered: 10/18/2023)\n10/23/2023 Minute Entry for proceedings held before Judge Carl J. Nichols: Hearing on Conditions of Release as to JASON HANIF REHMAN held on 10/23/2023. Motion 18 Granted. Further Order to be issued by the Court. Status\nConference set for 11/6/2023 at 11:00 AM in Telephonic/VTC before Judge Carl J. Nichols. Bond Status of Defendant: Defendant remains on Personal Recognizance; Court Reporter: Lorraine Herman; Defense Attorney:\nEugene Ohm; US Attorney: Caroline Burrell; Pretrial Officer: Christine Schuck. (zcam) (Entered: 10/23/2023)\n10/24/2023 20 NOTICE of Filing (Proposed Order) by JASON HANIF REHMAN re 18 Unopposed MOTION to Modify Conditions of Release (Attachments: # 1 Text of Proposed Order)(Ohm, Eugene) (Entered: 10/24/2023)\n10/25/2023 21 Emergency MOTION to Modify Conditions of Release (Unopposed) by JASON HANIF REHMAN. (Attachments: # 1 Text of Proposed Order)(Ohm, Eugene) (Entered: 10/25/2023)\n10/26/2023 ORDER MINUTE ORDER. The 21 Unopposed Motion to Temporarily Modify Conditions of Release is GRANTED. It is further ORDERED that the defendant may leave his home on Friday, October 27, 2023 in order to\nparticipate in an interview with his prospective employer in Arundel County. Signed by Judge Carl J. Nichols on October 26, 2023. (lccjn2) (Entered: 10/26/2023)\n10/26/2023 22 ORDER on 18 Motion to Modify Conditions of Release. Signed by Judge Carl J. Nichols on October 26, 2023. (lccjn2) (Entered: 10/26/2023)\n11/06/2023 Set/Reset Hearings as to JASON HANIF REHMAN: Status Conference RESET for 11/7/2023 at 01:00 PM in Telephonic/VTC before Judge Carl J. Nichols. (zcam) (Entered: 11/06/2023)\n11/07/2023 Minute Entry for proceedings held before Judge Carl J. Nichols: Hearing on Conditions of Release as to JASON HANIF REHMAN held on 11/7/2023. Defendant's Conditions of Release and Stay Away Order are\nmodified. Further Order to be issued by the Court. Bond Status of Defendant: Defendant remains on Personal Recognizance; Court Reporter: Lorraine Herman; Defense Attorney: Eugene Ohm; US Attorney: Caroline\nBurrell; Pretrial Officer: Christine Schuck. (zcam) (Entered: 11/07/2023)\n11/07/2023 MINUTE ORDER as to JASON HANIF REHMAN. It is ORDERED that the defendant may now reside at the new address verified by Pretrial Services. It is further ORDERED that Mr. Ahseem Patterson is installed as an\nadditional third-party custodian. It is further ORDERED that the stayaway order requiring Mr. Rehman to stay away from children is modified so that Mr. Rehman is required to stay away from children, except for the\nchildren of his immediate relatives. So ORDERED by Judge Carl J. Nichols on November 7, 2023. (lccjn2) (Entered: 11/07/2023)\n11/20/2023 24 Unopposed MOTION to Modify Conditions of Release by JASON HANIF REHMAN. (Attachments: # 1 Text of Proposed Order)(Ohm, Eugene) (Entered: 11/20/2023)\n12/01/2023 Set/Reset Hearings as to JASON HANIF REHMAN: Status Conference reset for 1/17/2024 at 12:30 PM in Telephonic/VTC before Judge Carl J. Nichols. (zcam) (Entered: 12/01/2023)\n12/06/2023 MINUTE ORDER as to JASON REHMAN. Defendant's 24 Unopposed Motion for Modification of Release Conditions is GRANTED. It is further ORDERED that Pretrial Services Officer Christine Schuck is authorized\nto approve travel by Defendant to visit his uncle in his uncles nursing facility. So ORDERED by Judge Carl J. Nichols on December 6, 2023. (lccjn2) (Entered: 12/06/2023)\n01/11/2024 26 Consent MOTION to Continue Status Hearing, Consent MOTION to Exclude Time Under the Speedy Trial Act by JASON HANIF REHMAN. (Attachments: # 1 Text of Proposed Order)(Ohm, Eugene) (Entered:\n01/11/2024)\n01/17/2024 MINUTE ORDER as to JASON HANIF REHMAN. The Consent Motion to Continue Status and Exclude Time Under The Speedy Trial Act is GRANTED. It is further Ordered that the parties shall contact the Deputy\nClerk to schedule another hearing in the next sixty days. It is further ORDERED that the period from January 17, 2024 until the next hearing date shall be excluded from computing the time within which a trial must\ncommence under the Speedy Trial Act because the ends of justice served by such a continuance outweigh the interests of the public and Defendant in a speedy trial. So ORDERED by Judge Carl J. Nichols on January 17,\n2024. (lccjn2) (Entered: 01/17/2024)\n01/19/2024 Set/Reset Hearings as to JASON HANIF REHMAN: Status Conference reset for 4/11/2024 at 12:30 PM in Courtroom 17- In Person before Judge Carl J. Nichols. (zcam) (Entered: 01/19/2024)\n04/08/2024 27 Consent MOTION to Continue Status Hearing, Consent MOTION to Exclude Time Under the Speedy Trial Act by JASON HANIF REHMAN. (Attachments: # 1 Text of Proposed Order)(Ohm, Eugene) (Entered:\n04/08/2024)\n04/11/2024 MINUTE ORDER. The 27 Motion to Continue is GRANTED. It is further ORDERED that the status hearing scheduled for April 11, 2024 is continued to May 22, 2024 at 12:30 PM. It is further ORDERED that the period\nfrom April 11, 2024 to May 23, 2024 shall be excluded from computing the time within which a trial must commence under the Speedy Trial Act because the ends of justice served by such a continuance outweigh the\ninterests of the public and Defendant in a speedy Trial. SO ORDERED by Judge Carl J. Nichols on April 11, 2024. (lccjn2) (Entered: 04/11/2024)\n05/10/2024 29 Consent MOTION to Continue Status Hearing, Consent MOTION to Exclude Time Under the Speedy Trial Act by JASON HANIF REHMAN. (Attachments: # 1 Text of Proposed Order)(Ohm, Eugene) (Entered:\n05/10/2024)\n05/20/2024 MINUTE ORDER. The 29 Motion to Continue is GRANTED. It is further ORDERED that the status hearing scheduled for May 22, 2024 is continued to July 11, 2024 at 4:30 PM. It is further ORDERED that the period\nfrom May 22, 2024 to July 11, 2024 shall be excluded from computing the time within which a trial must commence under the Speedy Trial Act because the ends of justice served by such a continuance outweigh the\ninterests of the public and Defendant in a speedy Trial. So ORDERED by Judge Carl J. Nichols on May 20, 2024. (lccjn2) (Entered: 05/20/2024)\n06/13/2024 31 Unopposed MOTION to Modify Conditions of Release by JASON HANIF REHMAN. (Attachments: # 1 Text of Proposed Order)(Ohm, Eugene) (Entered: 06/13/2024)\n06/14/2024 MINUTE ORDER as to JASON HANIF REHMAN. The 31 Unopposed Motion to Modify Conditions of Release is GRANTED. It is further ORDERED that Mr. Rehman's conditions of release are modified to authorize\nhim to attend a funeral inSilver Spring, MD on June 18, 2024 from 9:45 am to 2:30 pm. So ORDERED by Judge Carl J. Nichols on June 14, 2024. (lccjn2) (Entered: 06/14/2024)\n07/09/2024 33 Consent MOTION to Continue Status Hearing and Exclude Time Under the Speedy Trial Act by JASON HANIF REHMAN. (Attachments: # 1 Text of Proposed Order)(Ohm, Eugene) Modified text on 7/10/2024 (zstd).\n(Entered: 07/09/2024)\n07/10/2024 34 Joint MOTION to Continue Hearing by 60 Days and Exclude Time by USA as to JASON HANIF REHMAN. (Carrasco-Riley, Angelica) (Entered: 07/10/2024)\n07/10/2024 35 MOTION to Exclude Time by USA as to JASON HANIF REHMAN. (See docket entry 34 to view document.) (zstd) (Entered: 07/10/2024)\n07/11/2024 MINUTE ORDER. The 34 Joint Motion to Continue and the 35 Motion to Exclude Time are GRANTED and the 33 Consent Motion to Continue is DENIED as moot. It is further ORDERED that the status hearing\nscheduled for July 11, 2024 is vacated. It is further ORDERED that the Parties shall appear for a change of plea hearing at 12:30 on September 12, 2024. It is further ORDERED that the period from July 11, 2024 to\nSeptember 12, 2024 shall be excluded from computing the time within which a trial must commence under the Speedy Trial Act because the ends of justice served by such a continuance outweigh the interests of the public\nand Defendant in a speedy Trial. So ORDERED by Judge Carl J. Nichols on July 11, 2024. (lccjn2) (Entered: 07/11/2024)\n07/11/2024 Terminate Deadlines and Hearings as to JASON HANIF REHMAN: Status Conference set for 7/11/2024 is terminated pursuant to Minute Order filed 7/11/2024. (zcam) (Entered: 07/11/2024)\n07/17/2024 36 MOTION to Modify Conditions of Release by JASON HANIF REHMAN. (Attachments: # 1 Text of Proposed Order)(Ohm, Eugene) (Entered: 07/17/2024)\n08/06/2024 MINUTE ORDER as to JASON REHMAN. The 36 Motion to Modify Conditions of Release is DENIED. Based on the information available to the Court, Rehman has not demonstrated that the requested modification is\nwarranted. So ORDERED by Judge Carl J. Nichols on August 6, 2024. (lccjn2) (Entered: 08/06/2024)\n08/14/2024 37 Consent MOTION to Continue , Consent MOTION to Exclude Time Under the Speedy Trial Act by JASON HANIF REHMAN. (Attachments: # 1 Text of Proposed Order)(Ohm, Eugene) (Entered: 08/14/2024)\n09/03/2024 NOTICE OF HEARING as to JASON HANIF REHMAN: Plea Agreement Hearing reset for 10/8/2024 at 04:00 PM in Courtroom 17- In Person before Judge Carl J. Nichols. (zcam) (Entered: 09/03/2024)\n10/02/2024 38 Consent MOTION to Continue Hearing, Consent MOTION to Exclude Time Under the Speedy Trial Act by JASON HANIF REHMAN. (Attachments: # 1 Text of Proposed Order)(Ohm, Eugene) (Entered: 10/02/2024)\n10/07/2024 MINUTE ORDER as to JASON HANIF REHMAN. The 38 Consent Motion to Continue is GRANTED. It is hereby ORDERED that the plea hearing set for October 8, 2024, is vacated. The hearing shall be rescheduled\nonce the parties have informed the Court of their availability. So ORDERED by Judge Carl J. Nichols on October 7, 2024. (lccjn2) (Entered: 10/07/2024)\n10/21/2024 39 MOTION to Modify Conditions of Release (Time-Sensitive) by JASON HANIF REHMAN. (Attachments: # 1 Text of Proposed Order)(Ohm, Eugene) (Entered: 10/21/2024)\n10/21/2024 MINUTE ORDER as to JASON HANIF REHMAN. Upon consideration of the 39 Motion to Modify Conditions of Release, it is hereby ORDERED that the motion is granted. Defendant is hereby permitted to pick up his\nmother from Dulles International Airport and transport her to his aunt's funeral between 2:00 PM and 8:00 PM on October 24, 2024. It is further ORDERED that the parties shall appear for a change-of-plea hearing at 4:00\nPM on November 21, 2024, in Courtroom 17. It is further ORDERED that the period from September 12, 2024, to November 21, 2024, shall be excluded from computing the time within which a trial must commence\nunder the Speedy Trial Act because the ends of justice served by such a continuance outweigh the interests of the public and Defendant in a speedy trial. So ORDERED by Judge Carl J. Nichols on October 21, 2024.\n(lccjn2) (Entered: 10/21/2024)\n11/21/2024 Minute Entry for proceeding held on 11/21/2024 before Judge Carl J. Nichols: Plea Agreement Hearing as to JASON HANIF REHMAN on Count 1 of the Indictment filed on 3/2/2023. Plea of GUILTY entered by JASON\nHANIF REHMAN as to Count 1. REFERRAL TO PROBATION OFFICE for Presentence Investigation. Governments Sentencing Memorandum due by 3/6/2025. Defense Response to Sentencing Memorandums due by\n3/10/2025. Sentencing set for 3/13/2025 at 12:30 PM in Courtroom 17- In Person before Judge Carl J. Nichols. Governments oral motion to step back defendant; heard and taken under advisement. Supplemental brief is\ndue by 11/25/2024 at 5:00 pm. Bond Status of Defendant: Continued on Personal Recognizance; Defense Attorney: Eugene Kim Ohm; US Attorney: Caroline Burrell; Court Reporter: Sherry Lindsay. (zed) (Entered:\n11/21/2024)\n11/21/2024 41 PLEA AGREEMENT as to JASON HANIF REHMAN. (zed) (Entered: 11/21/2024)\n11/21/2024 42 STATEMENT OF OFFENSE by USA as to JASON HANIF REHMAN. (zed) (Entered: 11/21/2024)\n11/21/2024 43 WAIVER of Trial by Jury as to JASON HANIF REHMAN. Approved by Judge Carl J. Nichols on 11/21/2024. (zed) (Entered: 11/21/2024)\n11/25/2024 44 MOTION for Release from Custody by JASON HANIF REHMAN. (Attachments: # 1 Exhibit, # 2 Exhibit)(Ohm, Eugene) (Entered: 11/25/2024)\n11/26/2024 45 Unopposed MOTION to Modify Conditions of Release by JASON HANIF REHMAN. (Attachments: # 1 Text of Proposed Order)(Ohm, Eugene) (Entered: 11/26/2024)\n11/27/2024 MINUTE ORDER as to JASON HANIF REHMAN. The 45 Unopposed Motion is GRANTED. Defendant is hereby permitted to visit his sisters home in Rockville, Maryland, on November 28, 2024, from 2:00 PM to\n11:00 PM. So ORDERED by Judge Carl J. Nichols on November 27, 2024. (lccjn2) (Entered: 11/27/2024)\n01/13/2025 46 Consent MOTION to Continue by JASON HANIF REHMAN. (Attachments: # 1 Text of Proposed Order)(Ohm, Eugene) (Entered: 01/13/2025)\n01/14/2025 MINUTE ORDER as to JASON HANIF REHMAN. The 44 Motion for Release from Custody is DENIED. The Court concludes that Defendants circumstances are not \"exceptional\" for purposes of 18 U.S.C. \u00a7 3145(c), so\n18 U.S.C. \u00a7 3143(a)(2) requires the Court to order that Defendant be detained pending sentencing. So ORDERED by Judge Carl J. Nichols on January 14, 2025. (lccjn2) (Entered: 01/14/2025)\n01/14/2025 MINUTE ORDER as to JASON HANIF REHMAN. The 46 Consent Motion to Continue is GRANTED. The sentencing hearing scheduled for March 13, 2025, is hereby rescheduled to June 12, 2025, at 12:00 PM. The\ngovernment shall file its sentencing memorandum on or before June 5, 2025. Defendant shall file his sentencing memorandum on or before June 9, 2025. So ORDERED by Judge Carl J. Nichols on January 14, 2025.\n(lccjn2) (Entered: 01/14/2025)\n01/14/2025 Set/Reset Deadlines/Hearings as to JASON HANIF REHMAN: Government Sentencing Memorandum due by 6/5/2025. Defense Sentencing Memorandum due by 6/9/2025. Sentencing reset for 6/12/2025 at 12:00 PM in\nCourtroom 17- In Person before Judge Carl J. Nichols. (zcam) (Entered: 03/10/2025)\n01/16/2025 47 STATUS REPORT (Minute Order - 1/14/25) by JASON HANIF REHMAN (Ohm, Eugene) (Entered: 01/16/2025)\n01/16/2025 MINUTE ORDER as to JASON HANIF REHMAN. Upon consideration of the 47 Status Report, the Court ORDERS Defendant to self-surrender by February 19, 2025. So ORDERED by Judge Carl J. Nichols on January\n16, 2025. (lccjn2) (Entered: 01/16/2025)\n02/13/2025 48 Unopposed MOTION to Modify Conditions of Release (Temporarily), Unopposed MOTION for Extension of Time to Self-Surrender by JASON HANIF REHMAN. (Attachments: # 1 Text of Proposed Order)(Ohm,\nEugene) (Entered: 02/13/2025)\n02/14/2025 MINUTE ORDER as to JASON HANIF REHMAN. The 48 Unopposed Motion is GRANTED. Defendant is hereby permitted to attend the services specified in the motion from 8:00 AM to 3:00 PM on February 16, 2025.\nIt is further ORDERED that Defendants self-surrender date be extended to March 3, 2025. So ORDERED by Judge Carl J. Nichols on February 14, 2025. (lccjn2) (Entered: 02/14/2025)\n06/05/2025 53 SENTENCING MEMORANDUM by USA as to JASON HANIF REHMAN (Burrell, Caroline) (Entered: 06/05/2025)\n06/09/2025 54 SENTENCING MEMORANDUM by JASON HANIF REHMAN (Attachments: # 1 Exhibit, # 2 Exhibit, # 3 Exhibit, # 4 Exhibit, # 5 Exhibit, # 6 Exhibit, # 7 Exhibit, # 8 Exhibit, # 9 Exhibit, # 10 Exhibit, # 11 Exhibit, #\n12 Exhibit, # 13 Exhibit, # 14 Exhibit, # 15 Exhibit, # 16 Exhibit, # 17 Exhibit, # 18 Exhibit, # 19 Exhibit, # 20 Exhibit, # 21 Exhibit, # 22 Exhibit)(Ohm, Eugene) (Entered: 06/09/2025)\n06/13/2025 Set/Reset Hearings as to JASON HANIF REHMAN: Sentencing reset for 6/18/2024 at 11:00 AM in Courtroom 17- In Person before Judge Carl J. Nichols. (zcam) (Entered: 06/13/2025)\n06/18/2025 56 NOTICE of Proposed Order of Forfeiture by USA as to JASON HANIF REHMAN (Burrell, Caroline) (Entered: 06/18/2025)\n06/18/2025 Minute Entry for proceedings held before Judge Carl J. Nichols: Sentencing held on 6/18/2025 as to JASON HANIF REHMAN as to Count 1. Defendant sentenced to One Hundred Sixty-eight (168) months of\nIncarceration, followed by Ten (10) years of Supervised Release (with conditions). $100 Special Assessment. Bond Status of Defendant: Committed/Commitment Issued; Court Reporter: Tammy Nestor; Defense Attorney:\nEugene Jeen-Young Kim Ohm; US Attorneys: Angelica Carrasco-Riley and Caroline Burrell; Probation Officer: Kelli Willett; Defense Witnesses: Zaheer Rehman, Lori Shah, and Aneela Patterson. (zkh) (Entered:\n06/18/2025)\n06/18/2025 57 Unopposed MOTION to Dismiss Count Two, Three, and Four by USA as to JASON HANIF REHMAN. (Burrell, Caroline) (Entered: 06/18/2025)\n06/18/2025 59 LETTER by JASON HANIF REHMAN. \"Leave to file granted\" by Judge Carl J. Nichols on 6/18/2025. (zstd) (Entered: 06/23/2025)\n06/20/2025 58 ORDER DIRECTING FORFEITURE OF PROPERTY as to JASON HANIF REHMAN. Signed by Judge Carl J. Nichols on June 20, 2025. (lccjn2) (Entered: 06/20/2025)\n07/02/2025 60 ORDER GRANTING 57 Unopposed Motion to Dismiss Counts as to JASON HANIF REHMAN. Signed by Judge Carl J. Nichols on July 2, 2025. (lccjn2) (Entered: 07/02/2025)\n07/02/2025 DISMISSAL OF COUNTS on Government Motion as to JASON HANIF REHMAN. (zstd) (Entered: 07/03/2025)\n07/18/2025 61 JUDGMENT as to JASON HANIF REHMAN. Statement of Reasons Not Included. Signed by Judge Carl J. Nichols on 7/18/2025. (zstd) (Entered: 07/18/2025)\n07/18/2025 62 STATEMENT OF REASONS as to JASON HANIF REHMAN re 61 Judgment Access to the PDF Document is restricted per Judicial Conference Policy. Access is limited to Counsel of Record and the Court. Signed by\nJudge Carl J. Nichols on 7/18/2025. (zstd) (Entered: 07/18/2025)\n12/08/2025 63 MOTION for Compassionate Release by JASON HANIF REHMAN. (zstd) (Entered: 12/11/2025)\n12/16/2025 64 NOTICE OF ATTORNEY APPEARANCE Shehzad Akhtar appearing for USA. (Akhtar, Shehzad) (Entered: 12/16/2025)\n12/16/2025 65 MOTION for Extension of Time to File Response/Reply as to 63 MOTION for Compassionate Release by USA as to JASON HANIF REHMAN. (Akhtar, Shehzad) (Entered: 12/16/2025)\n12/22/2025 MINUTE ORDER as to JASON HANIF REHMAN. Upon consideration of the 65 Motion for Extension of Time, that Motion is GRANTED. The government shall file a response to the 63 Motion for Compassionate\nRelease on or before January 21, 2026. So ORDERED by Judge Carl J. Nichols on 12/22/2025. (lccjn2) (Entered: 12/22/2025)\n01/21/2026 66 Memorandum in Opposition by USA as to JASON HANIF REHMAN re 63 MOTION for Compassionate Release (Akhtar, Shehzad) (Entered: 01/21/2026)\n02/02/2026 67 NOTICE OF ATTORNEY APPEARANCE Rick E. Blaylock, Jr appearing for USA. (Blaylock, Rick) (Main Document 67 replaced at request of the filer on 2/2/2026) (zmcg). (Entered: 02/02/2026)\n02/02/2026 68 NOTICE of Service by Publication by USA as to JASON HANIF REHMAN (Attachments: # 1 Exhibit)(Blaylock, Rick) (Entered: 02/02/2026)\n02/02/2026 69 REQUEST FOR LEAVE TO FILE REVIEW as to JASON HANIF REHMAN. The attached document requires leave to file: Mr. Rehman's Motion. Reason(s): Other- Pro Se Filer. (zstd) (Entered: 02/04/2026)\n02/02/2026 MINUTE ORDER as to JASON HANIF REHMAN. Upon consideration of the 69 Motion for Extension of Time, it is hereby ORDERED that Defendant is granted leave to file that Motion and other filings associated with\nhis 63 Motion for Compassionate Release. The 69 Motion for Extension of Time shall therefore be deemed to have been properly filed, and the Clerk is directed to file the attached document on the public docket. It is\nfurther ORDERED that the 69 Motion for Extension of Time is GRANTED nunc pro tunc. Defendant shall file a reply on or before March 14, 2026. So ORDERED by Judge Carl J. Nichols on 02/05/2026. (lccjn2)\n(Entered: 02/05/2026)\n02/02/2026 70 MOTION for Extension of Time to File Response/Reply as to 63 MOTION for Compassionate Release by JASON HANIF REHMAN. (zstd) (Entered: 02/05/2026)\n03/09/2026 71 REPLY TO OPPOSITION to Motion by JASON HANIF REHMAN re 63 MOTION for Compassionate Release (Attachments: # 1 Letters of Support)(zstd) (Entered: 03/13/2026)\nPACER Service Center\nTransaction Receipt\n06/12